{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/95893-changing-lineages-in-game","id":95893,"title":"changing lineages in game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-21T13:10:37-07:00","id":95893,"title":"changing lineages in game.","content":"Is it possible to change from a frakenstain to an unfleshed in game... jw cuz promethen can make other ones and franken can re equip limbs.? someone help.??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2562-zach23743","name":"zach23743","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:15:48-07:00","id":95898,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to change from a frakenstain to an unfleshed in game... jw cuz promethen can make other ones and franken can re equip limbs.? someone help.??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2562-zach23743","name":"zach23743","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:17:55-07:00","id":95904,"title":"","content":"No, for much the same reason it's not possible to change species. Your Lineage, as the name indicates, is the type of freaky corpse-robot you draw creative line-of-descent from, and because of how causality works your ancestry is not remotely likely to change in the course of typical events.<br /> <br /> This goes double when discussing a shift from corpse-robot to non-corpse robot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:29:17-07:00","id":95917,"title":"","content":"But u can change from most things back to mortals. why not go to unfleshed from frankenstain... the unfleshed has no technical lineage.. is a unclassified class and if it came up to story could it be an idea? like a changling could become a vampire sense they r technically mortal. like mages...tho abominations r not widly talked about in wod","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2562-zach23743","name":"zach23743","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:20:13-07:00","id":95951,"title":"","content":"Neither Changelings or Magi can become vampires. They just die.<br /> <br /> But if you have a good idea for how it would happen, why not? Do you have one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:45:23-07:00","id":95966,"title":"","content":"They can't just die or all humans changed would die.? Thts why wod has the abominations term. like all vampires and mages and changlings were human then awakened to new. Vampires can become human gain... prometheans try to be human but r undead...and frankenstain r almost zombie right and they fall apart with enough damage but can put themselves back together... and if prometheans die they come back at los to azoth. unless u have the bistowment. right? And prometheans can make others right? so why couldn't u make a new hole body (unfleshed) fuse it with your own brain by dieing. sense frankenstain can get the bistowment to attach new limbs (why not body) and your fire to bring to life... and the unfleshed need nothing more then first dose of oil for the fluids to come to life. why can't a frank become an unleashed with humanish brain but maybe upgraded. (sense it does say in the book tht the unleashed even has tech before its age.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2562-zach23743","name":"zach23743","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:48:34-07:00","id":95968,"title":"","content":"Js cuz i wanna change classes with out los to my stats... so im trying for back doors and unwritten things. and ik alt of wod is story teller discussion so im trying to come up with a legit argument. yea know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2562-zach23743","name":"zach23743","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T17:38:37-07:00","id":96077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zach23743</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/95893-changing-lineages-in-game?p=95966#post95966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't just die or all humans changed would die.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages and changelings are not humans that vampires can turn into other vampires. The metaphysics don't work that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thts why wod has the abominations term. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Abomination&quot; is not a term in the nWoD. You're thinking of cWoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires can become human gain\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Unconfirmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> prometheans try to be human but r undead </div> </div> </div>Not-truly-living. There's a number of differences, chief among them being that you can still kill a Promethean through poison, deprivation and disease.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and frankenstain r almost zombie right </div> </div> </div>In the same sense that my leather jacket would be a zombie if you gave it sentience and mobility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if prometheans die they come back at los to azoth. </div> </div> </div>Once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And prometheans can make others right? so why couldn't u make a new hole body (unfleshed) fuse it with your own brain by dieing. sense frankenstain can get the bistowment to attach new limbs (why not body) and your fire to bring to life... and the unfleshed need nothing more then first dose of oil for the fluids to come to life. why can't a frank become an unleashed with humanish brain but maybe upgraded. (sense it does say in the book tht the unleashed even has tech before its age.) </div> </div> </div>Because the Wretched are patchwork people made of human parts and bits of other materials holding them together. Putting a human brain in a metal body doesn't change that - look at Magnum Opus's rules for Constructs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zach23743</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/95893-changing-lineages-in-game?p=95968#post95968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Js cuz i wanna change classes with out los to my stats\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming this is a DnD analogy you're making\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Your Lineage is not your &quot;class.&quot; Your supernatural template is not your &quot;class.&quot; Your Refinement is the nearest you come to a &quot;class&quot; and there are rules explaining how to change it written right in the corebook. Your Lineage is your &quot;race.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so im trying for back doors and unwritten things. and ik alt of wod is story teller discussion so im trying to come up with a legit argument. yea know? </div> </div> </div>What is it about the Unfleshed that makes you want to change from a Frankenstein to one of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T14:53:55-07:00","id":119980,"title":"","content":"The rules as written &quot;RAW&quot; does not allow for changing your lineage. However a possibility exists that your promethean could become human and then have their corpse used to make a new promethean... That technically isn't the same character but it comes close.<br /> <br /> Of course you can home brew anything you want. Maybe there is some advanced alchemical ritual that allows you to change your lineage. Really it's your game and you should do what you would like with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}